  "fixture": "Public environment/path/UUID/time/version/receipt vectors only. Fresh real JVM negative tests. OPS uses fixed fake Java and local static unit syntax verification; no host manager/service/credential changes. FLOCK uses isolated retained regular files, real libc and util-linux2.41.3 with narrow native fault ports. No host lockfile, UID or service mutation.",
  "oracle": "051/PT221..232: bounded nonsecret canonical input, missing/null/unknown rejection, no parsing diagnostics, exact ASCII receipt after owned resource closure, 0/10/50/70 mapping, unexpected runtime escape/fixed fatal message, native admission negatives,64 independent invocations. 018/PT001..008: fixed receipt byte matrix and JVM exit override; all base directives and4 selected previous-key profiles; actual sh/ShellCheck/systemd-analyze with recorded outputs; release classpath/JDBC runtime/Java25 flags. 003/PT-OPS-FLOCK-001..008: independent flock exit20 while Java holds and Java empty while external holds; fcntl does not conflict; one of32 wins; retained original inode remains locked after path replacement; errno11 alone is contention; fixed open flags0x80000/flock6, close once and IO diagnostic redaction. 005/PT-OPS-LOCK-001..008: MaintenanceFileLock connects held directories/inode and real flock, requires euid0, root:root0755 directories, root:root0600 empty single-link file, RW tmpfs/access ACL absent, same device and re-open identity before/after callback. All native open/close positions and attributes/FS/ACL faults, null/runtime failure,32 simultaneous requests, no repair and fixed3 boot-only tmpfiles entries are checked. 007/PT-OPS-STOP-001..016: independent ASCII seven-property vectors, exact loaded/inactive/dead/no Job/zero PID admission; missing/duplicate/unknown/control/1024+1/null rejection; fixed API then Web fresh reads; interrupts preserved and64 concurrent invocations; fixed systemctl argv/5-second wait/1025-byte read; all three stdio close failures crossed with normal/exit/timeout/oversize/read/interrupt; child-only TERM and no force kill; empty inherited environment replaced with exact five nonsecret variables; actual unprovisioned host not-found states rejected. 009/PT-OPS-ENV-001..004: SS343 independent two-line ASCII golden; every byte changed to each other possible byte, missing/extra/duplicate/quoted/CRLF/unknown-key input, all128 UUID bit changes and +/-1 microsecond fail exact run binding; years0001/9999, null, caller-owned fresh arrays and64 concurrent results are independently checked. 011/PT-OPS-CFG-001..006: fixed static DB/version two-line ASCII grammar before Map parsing; literal rendered template, port1/65535 and database1/63, version1/16 and unique list65535/65536, wrong source/duplicate/unknown/alias/quotes/controls/high-byte/oversize/null rejection, fixed redaction and64 concurrent checks. Independent SS values, no production-generated expected. 013/PT-OPS-EFILE-001..008: real retained inode/channel reads with synthetic root/GID/local-FS metadata; exact source and run bytes, metadata types/modes/owner/group/link/size/device/ACL/FS before IO, max+1 bounded EOF and size/identity/time rechecks, same-name replacement rejection, explicit nine-key null/type matrix, every IO/owned-close occurrence, compound raw IO diagnostics stripped,64 reads and start/mid/final interrupts preserved. No source-derived expected or reflection into private production state. 015/PT-OPS-PFILE-001..008: real libc CREATE_NEW/NOFOLLOW/0600 and unchanged0640, literal content/mode/link oracle; inode ownership across name replacement, callback/close failures, null/invalid/closed rejection, no-replace publication and sync uncertainty without undo, one of32 concurrent publications with31 retained losers, unsupported default fails without mutation. Shared storage full-class coverage is from the full regression; these8 PT belong only to OPS. 017/PT-OPS-PUB-001..012: literal run bytes and0600 inode conditions, shared EFILE policy, CREATE_NEW plus native no-replace/fsync, bounded writes/readback, same-run re-force/reuse, different-run rejection, preexisting part preservation, same-run retirement with only initial ENOENT idempotence; independent full new/reuse/retire IO occurrence inventories, compound close diagnostics stripped, interrupts preserved, unknown runtime escape and32 serialized callers.",
  "limitations": "Scope covers private launcher, wrapper/unit syntax, low-level flock, borrowed-root admission/read/publish, read-only application stop observations and canonical environment bytes. Java coverage is not a shell percentage; shell decisions use recorded traces. Root UID/GID/tmpfs admission is synthetic over isolated real inodes; no privileged deployed service acceptance. Flock executes amd64 libc; aarch64 is ABI selection only and CLOEXEC is checked at the call boundary, not by inherited-FD inspection. Systemctl timeout tests use a process fault port, not a stalled manager or TERM-ignoring descendant. Borrowed-root publisher requires caller-held OS lock, stable namespace and terminal child; its success proves none of those. Failed unpublished parts remain for controlled operational reconciliation. Remaining gates: fixed namespace and trusted account resolution; OS lock continuity and child termination; durable authoritative run and parent lifecycle; real backup artifact and full cleanup callers; actual root systemd credential deployment; actual NK characterization and IT/ST.",
